  {
    id: 'uc2',
    title: '祖母的菜市场早晨',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 12,
    text: 'At fourteen I decided that selling vegetables was the easiest job in the world, and I asked my grandmother if I could ___1___ her for a morning. She agreed and let me sit behind her table. My first ___2___ walked away before I opened my mouth, and I saw my own ___3___ face in the window behind us. The hardest part was not the work but the ___4___ of waiting for someone to stop, so I gave up trying to sell and started to watch. She was never loud, yet her voice cut through the noise and found the people she wanted to ___5___. She did not simply hand over the tomatoes; she told buyers which ones would taste sweetest. When a boy asked for a free pepper, she gave him one with a smile. “Business,” she said, “is not only about ___6___; it is about whether people feel welcome when they leave.” By ten my throat was dry and my legs shook, but the line of people kept me in my ___7___. At noon a man with a restaurant nearby stopped and said that he needed a supplier he could ___8___. When he asked the price, my first large ___9___ was more than I had imagined, and on the way home the empty cart felt strangely ___10___. I understand now that patience and kindness are not soft qualities but a kind of ___11___ few people learn in a classroom. Her rules are still the ones I ___12___: listen before you speak, and look for the ___13___ behind every small action. Trust grows slowly, like a plant, and can be ruined in a single careless ___14___. That is the ___15___ I took from one hard morning on a plastic chair.',
    questions: [
      { n: 1, opts: ['answer', 'replace', 'help', 'forgive'], a: 2, explain: '上下文题。下文说我坐在桌后学着卖菜，说明我是去“帮忙”，不是替代或原谅她。' },
      { n: 2, opts: ['teacher', 'customer', 'officer', 'reporter'], a: 1, explain: '复现题。全文在菜市场卖菜，走到摊前又离开的人只能是顾客，与后文 buyers 同类。' },
      { n: 3, opts: ['helpless', 'careful', 'familiar', 'cheerful'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。我一句话没说就把人放走了，脸上的神情应是无助的，与后文手脚发麻同向。' },
      { n: 4, opts: ['fun', 'pain', 'noise', 'habit'], a: 1, explain: '逻辑关系题。not…but 构成对比，硬椅子与干渴的喉咙都是折磨，fun 方向相反。' },
      { n: 5, opts: ['miss', 'judge', 'follow', 'reach'], a: 3, explain: '固定搭配题。声音穿过喧闹“够得着”她想吸引的人，reach 与前句 found 呼应。' },
      { n: 6, opts: ['manners', 'profit', 'trouble', 'weather'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。祖母谈的是生意，not only 后接赚钱这一层，与 welcome 构成对比。' },
      { n: 7, opts: ['corner', 'window', 'chair', 'office'], a: 2, explain: '复现题。前文写我坐在桌后，末句又回到 plastic chair，人没走我只能继续坐着。' },
      { n: 8, opts: ['owe', 'punish', 'trust', 'suspect'], a: 2, explain: '上下文题。餐馆老板要找长期供货的人，关键在可靠；suspect 与 punish 与语境相反。' },
      { n: 9, opts: ['bill', 'order', 'menu', 'dish'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。整篮蔬菜被买走，说明这是我第一次接到大批 order（订货）；bill 是账单、menu 是菜单，都不合语境。' },
      { n: 10, opts: ['heavy', 'light', 'cold', 'slow'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。车已卖空却“奇怪地轻”，strangely 提示与前文的沉重形成反差。' },
      { n: 11, opts: ['problem', 'feeling', 'strength', 'secret'], a: 2, explain: '逻辑关系题。not…but 把耐心与善意从“软素质”翻转为一种真正的力量。' },
      { n: 12, opts: ['break', 'ignore', 'keep', 'change'], a: 2, explain: '固定搭配题。keep the rules 遵守规则，冒号后是她留下的两条规矩。' },
      { n: 13, opts: ['cost', 'reason', 'blame', 'danger'], a: 1, explain: '上下文题。先听再说，并寻找小动作背后的“原因”，与前句 listen before you speak 并列。' },
      { n: 14, opts: ['move', 'meal', 'stranger', 'morning'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。a careless move 一步疏忽；本句用植物的比喻说明信任毁于一时。' },
      { n: 15, opts: ['lesson', 'ticket', 'holiday', 'distance'], a: 0, explain: '复现题。全文收束在一个收获上：那一个早晨给我上的“一课”。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'uc3',
    title: '遗忘也是一种能力',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 12,
    text: 'Your brain does not keep everything that reaches it. While you sleep, it decides which events to keep and which to throw away. Scientists once called this cleaning a ___1___ of memory, but newer research says that forgetting is just as ___2___ as remembering. Researchers once trained mice to fear a certain sound. Some animals carried a changed gene that made forgetting impossible; a week later they still ___3___ the sound and could not move through the room. Dropping old information lets the brain concentrate on what matters now. If you kept every breakfast ever eaten, the ___4___ of finding the last one would be terrible. A student who reads a text again every day remembers ___5___ than one who waits three days, because the effort of ___6___ a half-faded memory makes it stronger. Forgetting also protects our feelings: the pain of a mistake fades faster than the skill it left behind. Without this slow washing, failures would stay bright forever and make any ___7___ painful. Some describe memory less as a ___8___ that records every event than as a muscle that grows when it is used. Sleep is the first ___9___, because the cleaning runs only in the quiet hours. Mood matters as well: people who feel safe ___10___ more of what they see. If one week of study seems to disappear, do not panic. Test yourself, sleep longer, and the missing part is easier to ___11___ than you expect. Fewer ___12___ readings and more active self-testing will serve you better. The aim is not a perfect record but a mind that holds what is useful and lets the rest ___13___ away. An empty afternoon then feels like part of the ___14___, because a brain that deletes well is a busy one, deciding where to spend its limited ___15___.',
    questions: [
      { n: 1, opts: ['weakness', 'treasure', 'decision', 'message'], a: 0, explain: '逻辑关系题。but newer research 把旧看法与今天的评价对照，过去人们把遗忘当作记忆的“缺陷”。' },
      { n: 2, opts: ['strange', 'useful', 'quick', 'hidden'], a: 1, explain: '复现题。as…as 把遗忘与记住并列，后文 also protects 继续说明遗忘同样有用。' },
      { n: 3, opts: ['enjoyed', 'ignored', 'feared', 'produced'], a: 2, explain: '上下文题。这些老鼠无法遗忘，一周后仍然害怕那个声音，前文 trained mice to fear 直接复现。' },
      { n: 4, opts: ['chance', 'prize', 'mystery', 'task'], a: 3, explain: '词义辨析题。记住所有早餐，反而要在海量记录里找最后一顿，成了一项糟糕的“任务”。' },
      { n: 5, opts: ['less', 'more', 'better', 'faster'], a: 0, explain: '逻辑关系题。than 前后对比，后句给出原因：费力提取才算真练习，天天重读记得更少。' },
      { n: 6, opts: ['printing', 'rebuilding', 'copying', 'avoiding'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。把半褪的记忆重新“搭建”起来才让它更牢，print 与 copy 都是不费力的重复。' },
      { n: 7, opts: ['risk-taking', 'homework', 'reading', 'sleeping'], a: 0, explain: '复现题。失败若永远鲜明，人就不敢再尝试，前句 a mistake 与本句 painful 指向冒险。' },
      { n: 8, opts: ['bridge', 'camera', 'library', 'engine'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。that records every event 是照相机式的记录，与后句 a muscle 形成对照。' },
      { n: 9, opts: ['proof', 'example', 'requirement', 'result'], a: 2, explain: '上下文题。本段讲你能控制的条件，睡眠排在第一位，是必要的“条件”而非结果。' },
      { n: 10, opts: ['forget', 'repeat', 'regret', 'remember'], a: 3, explain: '词义辨析题。情绪安全时人记得更多，主语 people who feel safe 决定方向。' },
      { n: 11, opts: ['recover', 'explain', 'prove', 'imagine'], a: 0, explain: '复现题。前文说一周的学习似乎消失了，消失的部分其实更容易重新找回。' },
      { n: 12, opts: ['careful', 'repeated', 'short', 'boring'], a: 1, explain: '复现题。全文反对天天重读，fewer 后接“重复的”阅读，与前文 every day 呼应。' },
      { n: 13, opts: ['pass', 'fly', 'wash', 'give'], a: 0, explain: '固定搭配题。holds what is useful 与 lets the rest pass away 对照，pass away 指自然消逝。' },
      { n: 14, opts: ['exam', 'plan', 'process', 'topic'], a: 2, explain: '复现题。文章开头把遗忘称为 this cleaning，一个空白的下午其实也是这一“过程”的一部分。' },
      { n: 15, opts: ['money', 'time', 'space', 'energy'], a: 3, explain: '固定搭配题。limited energy 指大脑把有限的“精力”投给该留下的事。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'uc4',
    title: '学校该不该只奖励第一名',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 12,
    text: 'Many schools put one student at the top of a list and invite the rest to watch. For years this seemed ___1___, because ranking is cheap and easy to explain to parents. Yet more teachers doubt that a prize shows how much a school has taught. A rank compares people who began from different places. When we praise the first and ignore the second, we measure not teaching but ___2___. If the top reward falls on whoever beat others, people are ___3___ to be used rather than trusted. Cooperation disappears from group work, since helping a weaker classmate brings no ___4___ to the helper. Outside school, work rarely rewards a single voice. A bridge needs engineers who write one shared report, and a ward needs nurses who pass information ___5___ to doctors. There the question is whether a team can turn a mistake into a plan before it becomes a ___6___. The answer is not to throw away testing: exams show what has not been ___7___. What should change is the number of prizes and the ___8___ behind each one. A school can reward progress and the essay rewritten after ___9___. Growth is harder to measure than rank. Writing comments is harder than pointing at a ___10___, so many schools keep a system that is cheap and looks ___11___. A prize is a public statement about what we value: one name placed in front of a hundred others. A better school would give fewer medals and room for a quiet ___12___: letting a classmate finish a sentence. Such a school produces adults who can be ___13___ in a room full of strangers. That is what an education should ___14___, and the ___15___ a school makes about what it wants to become.',
    questions: [
      { n: 1, opts: ['reasonable', 'strange', 'secret', 'dangerous'], a: 0, explain: '逻辑关系题。because 给出理由：排名便宜、快捷、好向家长解释，所以多年人们觉得它合理。' },
      { n: 2, opts: ['effort', 'money', 'courage', 'luck'], a: 3, explain: '上下文题。前句说排名比的是起点不同的学生，我们夸的其实是运气，而不是教学。' },
      { n: 3, opts: ['tools', 'friends', 'models', 'judges'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。rather than trusted 给出反义对照，被“使用”的只能是工具。' },
      { n: 4, opts: ['answer', 'punishment', 'chance', 'praise'], a: 3, explain: '复现题。本段讲的是奖励，帮同学要花时间又不会带来荣誉，praise 与 reward 同义复现。' },
      { n: 5, opts: ['politely', 'directly', 'secretly', 'lazily'], a: 1, explain: '上下文题。病房靠护士把信息“直接”交给医生，说明团队需要清楚的交接。' },
      { n: 6, opts: ['plan', 'disaster', 'success', 'habit'], a: 1, explain: '逻辑关系题。turn a mistake into a plan 与 before it becomes a… 对照，错误没人纠正就成事故。' },
      { n: 7, opts: ['finished', 'repeated', 'understood', 'forgotten'], a: 2, explain: '词义辨析题。考试的作用是暴露哪些内容还没被“理解”，与本段谈论的教学相呼应。' },
      { n: 8, opts: ['rule', 'prize', 'message', 'test'], a: 2, explain: '复现题。上文说奖励会传递信息，该变的是奖品数量和每个奖品背后的 message。' },
      { n: 9, opts: ['competition', 'silence', 'practice', 'advice'], a: 3, explain: '词义辨析题。essay rewritten after advice 指按老师建议重写，本段主语是进步而非名次。' },
      { n: 10, opts: ['list', 'chart', 'window', 'partner'], a: 1, explain: '固定搭配题。point at a chart 指着图表，与 writing comments 对照，harder than 决定取舍。' },
      { n: 11, opts: ['hopeful', 'serious', 'costly', 'peaceful'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。旧系统省成本又“看起来严肃”，这正是它难以被替换的原因。' },
      { n: 12, opts: ['patience', 'bravery', 'honesty', 'curiosity'], a: 0, explain: '上下文题。冒号后解释：让同学把句子说完，这种品质是耐心。' },
      { n: 13, opts: ['hidden', 'heard', 'chosen', 'blamed'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。be heard in a room full of strangers 与全文“能说清自己的想法”呼应。' },
      { n: 14, opts: ['cost', 'refuse', 'copy', 'produce'], a: 3, explain: '复现题。上句 produces adults who… 是本段主旨，说明教育应当“产出”什么样的人。' },
      { n: 15, opts: ['report', 'promise', 'speech', 'letter'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。与前句 a public statement 同义，奖章是学校关于自己想成为怎样的社群所作的承诺。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'uc5',
    title: '一场辩论赛教会我的事',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 12,
    text: 'In my first school debate I believed that winning was a matter of talking well. I had forty notes and practised my opening line until it sounded like a ___1___. Chen Yu filled eleven pages with questions our opponents might raise, and I asked her to leave half her work to me. I did not notice that the other team finished each sentence before mine, and the hall ___2___ at my timing. By the third round our opponents were answering the questions Chen Yu had written, and every point carried a ___3___ from our school life. In the final round my notes were useless, because I had written speeches rather than ___4___. We came second, and Chen Yu said nothing on the bus home; that ___5___ was worse than any comment. I asked what she had done that I had not, and the answer was listening. She had sat for two weeks at the gate and in classrooms, writing down what people said when a rule made them ___6___. My forty notes were only opinions about my own ___7___. In the next term I learned to build my ___8___ before my voice. A shopkeeper told us why small shops close, and his numbers were more ___9___ than any chart in our textbook. What I had wanted was never a medal but the right to say something I could ___10___. Speaking is the part of thinking that others can see; if the part below is ___11___, it shakes at a real question. Her eleven pages beside my forty notes let the ___12___ speak. The habit she gave me is smaller than a skill and larger than a ___13___: before I change a ___14___, I ask the people inside it what they ___15___.',
    questions: [
      { n: 1, opts: ['question', 'poem', 'mistake', 'number'], a: 1, explain: '复现题。练到像“诗”一样顺口，与开头 line 押韵呼应，说明我只重形式。' },
      { n: 2, opts: ['wept', 'shouted', 'laughed', 'whispered'], a: 2, explain: '上下文题。对手先说完一句，全场哄笑我的时机，与后文 my notes were useless 相呼应。' },
      { n: 3, opts: ['warning', 'promise', 'joke', 'secret'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。对手每一点都像对我们自己生活的提醒，carry a warning from 表示警告意味。' },
      { n: 4, opts: ['speeches', 'questions', 'reasons', 'examples'], a: 1, explain: '逻辑关系题。rather than 对照：我写的是演讲稿，不是对手真会提出的问题，所以临场无用。' },
      { n: 5, opts: ['silence', 'letter', 'lesson', 'report'], a: 0, explain: '上下文题。她在回程车上一句话也没说，那份“沉默”比任何评价都难受。' },
      { n: 6, opts: ['proud', 'angry', 'curious', 'nervous'], a: 1, explain: '上下文题。她记下人们说起校规时的原话，只有让人不满的规则才需要这样解释。' },
      { n: 7, opts: ['kindness', 'luck', 'cleverness', 'courage'], a: 2, explain: '词义辨析题。与首段“我以为获胜只靠会说”相扣，我的笔记只是关于自己聪明的看法。' },
      { n: 8, opts: ['voice', 'ears', 'hands', 'eyes'], a: 1, explain: '复现题。build my ears before my voice：先听再说，是全篇转折的关键。' },
      { n: 9, opts: ['frightening', 'simple', 'encouraging', 'boring'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。小店一家接一家关门，这些数字比课本图表更令人心惊。' },
      { n: 10, opts: ['guess', 'forget', 'defend', 'repeat'], a: 2, explain: '固定搭配题。say something I could defend 说出能为之辩护的话，与前文论证的意象一致。' },
      { n: 11, opts: ['shallow', 'missing', 'clear', 'foreign'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。水面下的思考太浅，露出的部分一遇真问题就发抖。' },
      { n: 12, opts: ['distance', 'change', 'result', 'difference'], a: 3, explain: '固定搭配题。let the difference speak 让差距自己说话，指她那十一页与我那四十页之别。' },
      { n: 13, opts: ['problem', 'prize', 'money', 'gift'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。smaller than a skill and larger than a prize，与前文“我不再在意奖牌”同向。' },
      { n: 14, opts: ['rule', 'club', 'memory', 'habit'], a: 0, explain: '复现题。全文辩论围绕校规展开，change a rule 与后句 the people inside it 相扣。' },
      { n: 15, opts: ['fear', 'owe', 'hope', 'see'], a: 3, explain: '上下文题。改变规则之前先问身处其中的人“看到”什么，与前句 ask 构成宾语。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'uc6',
    title: '一本被弄丢的书',
    exam: '中考',
    mins: 10,
    text: 'Last term I lent my best friend a book, a birthday present from my grandfather that I had read four times. On Friday I asked her to bring it on Monday, for our reading class. She said yes and ___1___ her bag. On Monday she came to school without her ___2___. At break she walked up to me. “I cannot find the book. I looked in every corner of my room.” I felt my face go ___3___ and said nothing. I had lent it to her because I ___4___ her, but now I was not sure. For two days we did not speak. Then a boy from Class 3 came with the book. “I took it from the desk behind yours. I thought it was mine.” Holding the book, I thought of the two ___5___ days behind us. She could have said nothing and let me lose the ___6___ in class. When I told her, she did not laugh or ___7___ me. She only said, “I am glad it is back.” That evening I wrote on a card: thank you for being ___8___. Since then I ask two questions before I am angry. Is the story clear? Or is there another reason? A good ___9___ is not a guess; it is a habit of speaking first. One more question on Monday would have saved two days of feeling ___10___. My grandfather would have cared about ___11___ we treated each other, not about the book. The book now stays on my shelf, and I sometimes borrow her ___12___. Last Friday she asked me to read a new story, and I said yes without ___13___. I still keep her card. I do not use it for ___14___; it reminds me that friendship grows fastest in those who spend time ___15___.',
    questions: [
      { n: 1, opts: ['cleaned', 'closed', 'lost', 'forgot'], a: 1, explain: '上下文题。她答应了并合上书包，表示书已收进包里，为后文忘带埋下伏笔。' },
      { n: 2, opts: ['homework', 'umbrella', 'schoolbag', 'gloves'], a: 2, explain: '复现题。前一句刚提到书包，周一她来校却没带书包，书自然不在身边。' },
      { n: 3, opts: ['warm', 'pale', 'wide', 'busy'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。心爱的书丢了，脸色发白又不说话，pale 符合难过与生气的心情。' },
      { n: 4, opts: ['missed', 'trusted', 'thanked', 'followed'], a: 1, explain: '逻辑关系题。because 说明借书的原因是信任，but now I was not sure 构成转折。' },
      { n: 5, opts: ['sunny', 'short', 'quiet', 'noisy'], a: 2, explain: '上下文题。前句说两天我们谁也不说话，用 quiet 形容那段冷清的时光。' },
      { n: 6, opts: ['name', 'ticket', 'chance', 'seat'], a: 2, explain: '词义辨析题。她只要不说，我就会在阅读课上失去那次机会，lose the chance 与全文线索一致。' },
      { n: 7, opts: ['help', 'shout at', 'blame', 'wait for'], a: 2, explain: '词义辨析题。or 连接两种她都没有做的反应：既没笑我也没责怪我。' },
      { n: 8, opts: ['brave', 'polite', 'clever', 'honest'], a: 3, explain: '复现题。她主动来告知真相，卡片感谢的正是这份诚实。' },
      { n: 9, opts: ['question', 'friend', 'story', 'answer'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。分号后说它其实是一种先开口的习惯，主语只能是上文强调的“好问题”。' },
      { n: 10, opts: ['excited', 'sorry', 'tired', 'afraid'], a: 1, explain: '上下文题。冷战那两天我一直在自责，feeling sorry 指这段心情。' },
      { n: 11, opts: ['when', 'how', 'why', 'where'], a: 1, explain: '词义辨析题。祖父在意的不是书，而是我们彼此“怎样”相处，cared about 后接方式。' },
      { n: 12, opts: ['dictionary', 'pen', 'magazine', 'bag'], a: 3, explain: '复现题。风波之后我有时反而向她借东西，与开头的 her bag 呼应。' },
      { n: 13, opts: ['waiting', 'looking', 'asking', 'thinking'], a: 3, explain: '固定搭配题。said yes without thinking 不假思索地答应，说明信任已经恢复。' },
      { n: 14, opts: ['writing', 'reading', 'drawing', 'singing'], a: 0, explain: '词义辨析题。卡片不是拿来写字的，do not use it for writing 与后句 it reminds me 对照。' },
      { n: 15, opts: ['running', 'sharing', 'talking', 'listening'], a: 3, explain: '复现题。全文结论是愿意花时间倾听的人友情长得最快，呼应 speak first 与 question。' },
    ],
  },
